---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../data/legal";
import { links } from "../data/site";
---

<Legal
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="What this site is and is not: not therapy, not medical or legal advice, and not a crisis service. Plus how affiliate links and book sales work here."
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
  current="disclaimer"
>
  <div class="callout urgent">
    <p>
      <strong>This site is not a crisis service.</strong> Nobody monitors it for
      emergencies and messages are not read in real time. If you are in
      immediate danger, call <strong>911</strong>. If you need to speak to
      somebody now, the National Domestic Violence Hotline is{" "}
      <strong>1-800-799-7233</strong>, free and staffed 24 hours. More on the{" "}
      <a href="/resources">resources page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>This is not professional advice</h2>

  <p>
    HoneyBear Katherine's Haven is a podcast and this is its website. Katherine
    L. Carter is a writer, former teacher and community builder. She is{" "}
    <strong>not a licensed therapist, counsellor, psychologist, physician,
    lawyer, or financial adviser</strong>, and nothing published here is
    delivered in any of those capacities.
  </p>

  <p>
    Everything on this site — episodes, articles, and anything said live on air
    — is general commentary and personal opinion offered for information and
    encouragement. It is not a diagnosis, a treatment plan, legal guidance, or a
    substitute for care from a qualified professional who knows your situation.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>No professional relationship is created</strong> by reading this
    site, listening to an episode, attending a live show, or contacting
    Katherine. Please do not delay or disregard advice from a qualified
    professional because of something you read or heard here.
  </p>

  <h2>Your decisions are your own</h2>

  <p>
    Relationships are specific and we do not know yours. Only you can weigh what
    applies. Any action you take based on this site is taken at your own
    discretion and risk, and Katherine L. Carter accepts no liability for
    outcomes arising from it, to the fullest extent the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2>Safety information</h2>

  <p>
    The <a href="/harbor-of-hope">Harbor of Hope</a> and{" "}
    <a href="/resources">resources</a> pages list national organisations that
    provide crisis support, legal information and safety planning. Those
    organisations are independent. We do not run them, are not affiliated with
    them, and cannot influence what happens when you contact them.
  </p>

  <p>
    We list them because they are established and free. We check them
    periodically, but details change — if something here is out of date, please{" "}
    <a href="/contact">let us know</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>A note on the quick-exit button.</strong> The Harbor of Hope page
      has a control that moves you away quickly. It does not erase your browsing
      history, and it cannot protect you from monitoring software installed on
      your device. Please read the safety section on that page before relying on
      it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Guests and their views</h2>

  <p>
    Guests speak for themselves. Their appearance is not an endorsement of their
    views, work or business, and their views are not necessarily Katherine's.
    Similarly, links to other websites are provided for convenience — we do not
    control that content and are not responsible for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links and commercial relationships</h2>

  <p>
    In line with the US Federal Trade Commission's guidance on endorsements
    (16 CFR Part 255), here is exactly how money works on this site.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Link</th><th>Relationship</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>RYZE</strong></td>
        <td>Affiliate link. Katherine earns a commission if you buy, at no additional cost to you.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Pampered Chef</strong></td>
        <td>Katherine is an independent consultant and earns from orders placed through her page.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Weight of Dysfunction</strong></td>
        <td>Katherine is the author and earns royalties on sales. This is not an affiliate link and carries no tracking tag.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Cash App tip link</strong></td>
        <td>Voluntary support for the show. Nothing is unlocked or promised in return.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <strong>Everything on the <a href="/resources">resources page</a></strong>
        </td>
        <td>
          No commercial relationship of any kind. Nothing on that list pays to
          be there, and none of those links earn anything.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    We do not run advertising, do not accept payment for editorial coverage, and
    do not sell placement in articles. If that ever changes it will be disclosed
    here and on the page in question.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>

  <p>
    Articles are written carefully and reviewed before publication, but this is
    a podcast website, not a clinical reference. We do not guarantee that
    everything is complete or current, and we may update or correct pieces
    without notice. Where an article states something as fact, it is our
    understanding at the time of writing.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>

  <p>
    If anything here is unclear, or you think something on the site is wrong,{" "}
    <a href="/contact">get in touch</a> or email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
